    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive profile anchored by **Junior Caminero** (72.72) and **Trea Turner** (72.34), our highest-projected starters. **Junior Caminero** benefits from a high-leverage spot in the three-hole against a hittable opponent, while **Trea Turner** remains an elite start, buoyed by a favorable wind forecast and an advantageous matchup against Brown that mitigates the slight platoon drag. **Caleb Durbin** (70.67) also presents an elite play; his aggressive base-running upside, coupled with a generous park factor and a soft matchup against Johnson, R, makes him a primary engine for our category scarcity goals in stolen bases.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical hurdles in the outfield and behind the dish. While **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (67.03) serves as a strong play thanks to a significant park factor boost, **Yordan Alvarez** (52.19) and **Lars Nootbaar** (42.43) find themselves in riskier territory; **Yordan Alvarez** faces a difficult southpaw in S\u00e1nchez, C, suppressing his typically elite ceiling, and **Lars Nootbaar** is hampered by both a bottom-of-the-order assignment and a difficult platoon split. **Dillon Dingler** (46.25) barely clears our floor, remaining in the lineup primarily due to positional necessity rather than an overwhelming matchup. The most difficult bench decision involved **Chase Meidroth** (39.02), who missed the cut by less than a full point. Despite solid recent form, his suboptimal eighth-place batting order and the strength of the opposing arm ultimately pushed him below our 40.0 efficiency threshold. We will continue to monitor the weather and any late lineup shifts, particularly for those players like **Dillon Dingler** who are operating near the production floor.",
